## Examples

**Example — Data Pipeline (narrative format)**

Client: "ETL pipeline moving 50 M rows/day from legacy Oracle DB to Snowflake. Needs deduplication, schema mapping, and Slack alerting for failures."

Paragraph 1 — Approach: We recommend an async pipeline using Airbyte for extraction and dbt for transformation, deployed on AWS ECS. Schema mapping will require a one-week discovery sprint with the data team.

Paragraph 2 — Risks & effort: Oracle connectivity and legacy schema inconsistencies are the main risks (+20% buffer). Core effort: 120 h ingestion, 80 h transformation, 40 h monitoring, 30 h QA.

Paragraph 3 — Cost & team: Total 270 hours / 21 600 EUR. Timeline: 7 weeks. Team: 1 data engineer (lead) + 1 backend developer part-time.

